adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the code decrypts and parses incoming `keys` with:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

There is no `try/catch` around either `symmetricDecrypt(...)` or `JSON.parse(...)`. If the encryption key is missing/mismatched (note it falls back to `""`) or the decrypted plaintext is not valid JSON, either call can throw, resulting in an unhandled exception and an opaque 500 response from the Next.js API handler. This operational failure mode is directly present in the diff.
